  "description": "Species: Eucalyptus gunnii (Cider Gum)\rForm: Standard specimen\rLocation: 66 Castellain Road, rear (south) garden. This is the only tree in the garden.\r\rDescription of Works:\r\rCrown reduction and formative pruning of one mature Eucalyptus gunnii standard to reduce overall height by approximately 2?3 metres (not exceeding 25?30% of the live crown volume). Works to include selective shortening of extended upper and lateral branches to appropriate growth points in order to retain a balanced, natural crown form suitable to the species.\r\rRemoval of dead, dying, damaged and crossing branches throughout the crown.\rLight crown lift to achieve a clearance of approximately 2.5?3 metres above ground level, removing only secondary growth where necessary.\rAll pruning cuts to be made in accordance with current arboricultural best practice.\r\rReason for Works:\rTo manage overall size in relation to the property and neighbouring boundaries, reduce wind loading, maintain good arboricultural condition, and ensure continued safe retention of the tree within its setting.",
